=== PHASE B — Safe logging ===

B1. common/logging/safe-error.ts
- Add 'TimeoutError' and 'AbortError' to the `names` whitelist. Do not relax the regexes.
- Add `export function topStackFrame(error: unknown): string`:
  - read `error.stack` only if it is a string;
  - split into lines and keep those matching /^\s*at\s/;
  - on each, match /\(?((?:[A-Za-z]:)?[^():\s]+):(\d+):\d+\)?\s*$/;
  - skip frames whose path contains 'node_modules' or starts with 'node:';
  - normalise backslashes to '/';
  - keep the path from the last '/src/' or '/dist/' segment (inclusive, e.g. 'dist/modules/x/y.js'), otherwise the basename;
  - return `${path}:${line}`, or 'unknown';
  - never return anything from the message line.
- safe-error.spec.ts, new tests:
  - an Error whose message contains 'private@example.invalid' and a stack with a node_modules frame first then an app frame at F:\\x\\apps\\backend\\dist\\modules\\a\\b.js:12:5 → 'dist/modules/a/b.js:12';
  - a non-error → 'unknown';
  - safeErrorSummary({ name: 'TimeoutError' }) → 'kind=TimeoutError'.

B2. common/logging/safe-http.ts
- Add `export function routeProps(req: { route?: { path?: unknown } })`: return `{ routePattern: path }` when `req.route?.path` is a string, else `{}` (the empty object avoids a duplicate binding at request start).
- Add `export function healthAwareLogLevel(req: { url?: string }, res: { statusCode?: number }, err?: unknown)`:
  - err or status >= 500 → 'error';
  - status >= 400 → 'warn';
  - req.url starts with '/api/v1/health' → 'silent';
  - otherwise 'info'.
- safe-http.spec.ts: test both functions, including '/api/v1/health/ready' with 503 → 'error' (health failures are still logged), and a 200 health probe → 'silent'.

B3. config/config.schema.ts
